<Base title="German Lesson 5: Zählen" description="Self-paced beginner German lesson 5: Counting in German."><main class="lesson"><a class="back" href="/resources/german-async">← Back to the German learning path</a><p class="eyebrow">GERMAN · A1 · UNIT 1 · LESSON 05</p><h1 lang="de">Zählen</h1><p class="subtitle">Counting in German</p><p>Learn and practise numbers, listen to the examples, and test your understanding.</p><section class="panel"><h2>Watch and listen</h2><p>Use these videos to practise counting. Pause and repeat the numbers aloud.</p><div class="videos"><iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/TRjivsOxWZI" title="German counting video (YouTube)" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe><iframe src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/288173497?h=43e121c9e4" title="German counting video (Vimeo)" loading="lazy" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div></section><section class="panel"><h2>Numbers 0–20</h2><p>null, eins, zwei, drei, vier, fünf, sechs, sieben, acht, neun, zehn, elf, zwölf, dreizehn, vierzehn, fünfzehn, sechzehn, siebzehn, achtzehn, neunzehn, zwanzig.</p><p><strong>Tip:</strong> 16 is <em>sechzehn</em> and 17 is <em>siebzehn</em>.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Practise at your own pace</h2><ol><li>Count from zero to twenty, then backwards.</li><li>Say your age in German: Ich bin … Jahre alt.</li><li>Write the German words for 7, 12 and 19.</li></ol></section><nav class="lesson-nav"><a href="/resources/german-async">All lessons</a><a href="/resources/german-lesson-6">Next lesson →</a></nav></main></Base><style>.lesson{max-width:900px;margin:auto;padding:55px 24px 90px;color:#243d35}.back{font-size:.9rem;text-decoration:underline}.eyebrow{font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:700;margin-top:42px}h1{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(2.8rem,7vw,4.5rem);margin:12px 0}.subtitle{font-size:1.4rem;color:#567047}.lesson>p{line-height:1.7}.panel{margin-top:32px;background:#f7f6ee;border:1px solid #dce1d6;border-radius:20px;padding:28px}h2{font-size:1.35rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:16px}.videos{display:grid;gap:18px}iframe{width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/9;border:0;border-radius:12px}.vocab{list-style:none;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr));gap:12px}.vocab li{padding:12px;background:white;border-radius:10px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px}ol{padding-left:22px;line-height:2}.lesson-nav{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;margin-top:30px}.lesson-nav a{color:#304e3d;text-decoration:underline}</style>